  "id": "css-link-states-001",
  "assignment_version": 4,
  "title": "Link States",
  "prompt": "<p>Links change appearance for different states. Style the links on the page using the <strong>LVHA</strong> order (<strong>L</strong>ink, <strong>V</strong>isited, <strong>H</strong>over, <strong>A</strong>ctive) so later states can override earlier ones:</p><ol><li><code>a:link</code> — unvisited — <code>color: blue</code></li><li><code>a:visited</code> — visited — <code>color: purple</code></li><li><code>a:hover</code> — pointer over the link — <code>color: green</code></li><li><code>a:active</code> — while pressing — <code>color: red</code></li></ol><p>There are three links (<strong>W3C</strong>, <strong>MDN</strong>, and <strong>Master Programmer</strong>); the same rules should apply to all of them. After you Run, try hovering and clicking to see the states. Read more on <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Text_styling/Styling_links\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MDN: Styling links</a>.</p>",
  "files": {
    "html": {
      "mode": "readonly",
      "starter": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>Link States</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>Link States</h1>\n  <p><a id=\"w3c\" href=\"https://www.w3.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">W3C</a></p>\n  <p><a id=\"docs\" href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MDN</a></p>\n  <p><a id=\"master\" href=\"https://www.masterprogrammer.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Master Programmer</a></p>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    },
    "css": {
      "mode": "editable",
      "starter": "/* LVHA: Link, Visited, Hover, Active */\n\n"
    },
